# Top-level rspamd config overlay. Rspamd's main config does an implicit
# .include of $LOCAL_CONFDIR/rspamd.conf.local at the very top level
# (unlike local.d/, which only merges into sections matching the filename).
# This is the right home for directives that don't live inside any block.

# Rspamd 4 loads every top-level $LOCAL_CONFDIR/lua.local.d/*.lua file from
# rules/rspamd.lua. Do not also set the top-level `lua` option here: loading
# smg_ingest.lua twice registers duplicate coroutine symbols and can corrupt a
# concurrent milter callback, causing Postfix to receive an application error.
